1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,000
The launch date just slipped. Where on the Moon do you land now?

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Tell it where, when and what matters.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,500
Sun for power, Earth for comms, against the LOLA horizon.
1 km grid, 72 directions per pixel. The real run, played 6.8 times faster.

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:12,000
160,000 km², hour by hour. Scored in 15 s, in the browser.
Measured without screen capture: 14.8 s on 4 CPU cores, no GPU.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,800
Highest score, with its best landing window.

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,000
Sunlight left. Next night. When the Earth sets.

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Side by side with Artemis III candidate regions.

8
00:00:19,067 --> 00:00:21,600
Walk a 1:1 model of the site.
LOLA 240 m relief. Smaller craters and rocks are generated.

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,500
South Pole. North Pole. Whole Moon.
Poles: 1 km, date search. Whole Moon: 0.5°, fixed date.

10
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:28,000
Reference formulas checked against JPL Horizons: 0.002 arcminutes, at most.
Sun and Earth, azimuth and elevation. 726 comparisons at 3 south pole sites. Data: NASA LOLA, NASA/JPL SPICE DE440, LRO Diviner.

